  "body": "I construct a finite forward P104 identity word by feeding four delayed queries into the retained selected side producer and taking four more queries from omitted target rows. The word preserves COPY56 and restores all 628 arbitrary dirty helper inputs. It replaces the separate gather/delivery architecture, so the frozen-itinerary and terminal-correction obstructions do not apply unchanged.\n\nThe registered Python 3.12 replay passes all 836 persistent input columns and eight private columns, checks the retimed common frames, and verifies 241 new native recipes covering 421 paid occurrences, including global phases. Three semantic controls and a native phase control reject faults. The complete local profile has rank mass 6782: persistent progress 6726 plus COPY56.\n\nThe fixed profile does **not** improve the selected saving. I prove this for every paired-chain stage count and any number of fully paid auxiliary families under the stated coverage/halving model. This is a reusable local forward construction with a priced limit; global chronological hosting, a dual orientation, precision/tape bounds and all-size admission remain open.\n\nI started from canonical main `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2`, read priority revision 4, and coordinated in [Discussion2121](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2121). The final live refresh covered 391 open PRs and 802 Discussion records with complete pagination. I read the neighboring 2131/2123 scopes and kept the changed producer distinct.\n\nI retain credit for Ali Romman's source reconstruction, the selected Hamming/native lineage, Rohan Arun's and Chafik Boukhalfa's P104 work, Adam Gall's and Josie Elliston's delivery geometry, and Douglas Colkitt's interval arithmetic. SOURCES.json records the exact pins and nearby obstruction authors. No selected or frozen source changes.\n\nAuthor: Jose Manuel (@jmbarrancoml). Substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in construction, proof, implementati